#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:66
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:68
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kmines; is the classic Minesweeper game. You must uncover all the empty "
"squares without blowing up a mine."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you uncover a square, a number appears: it indicates how many mines "
"surround this square. If there is no number the neighboring squares are "
"automatically uncovered. When you find a square that you are sure contains a "
"mine, it is <emphasis>very</emphasis> useful to put a flag on it (by "
"right-clicking)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:79
#, no-c-format
msgid "How to Play"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You have to use the mouse and its three buttons to uncover or to flag the "
"squares (with two-buttoned mice, clicking the <mousebutton>middle</mousebutton> "
"button is generally achieved by simultaneously pressing the <mousebutton>"
"left</mousebutton> and the <mousebutton>right</mousebutton> "
"buttons). Here are the details:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <mousebutton>left</mousebutton> button will uncover a square. If there is a "
"bomb below that square, the bomb will explode, and the game will be over."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If there is not a bomb under the square, a number will appear. That is the "
"number of neighboring squares that contain bombs. <quote>Which ones?</quote> "
"you ask: That's the point of the game."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For each square (excluding edge and corner squares), there are 8 neighboring "
"squares."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If none of the neighboring squares has a bomb, then a blank will be shown under "
"the square, and all neighboring squares will be automatically uncovered."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:99
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<mousebutton>Left</mousebutton> clicking a flagged square is safe and does "
"nothing."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:101
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <mousebutton>right</mousebutton> button will mark a square as containing a "
"mine (by drawing a red flag on it) or, if the option is set, as being uncertain "
"(by drawing a question mark on it). The uncertain tag can be useful when you "
"are puzzled about the positions of mines."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <mousebutton>middle</mousebutton> button will clear the surrounding squares "
"if the right number of squares is already flagged. It is very useful since it "
"is much quicker than uncovering all individual squares."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:110
#, no-c-format
msgid "If your flags are not properly positioned, you will explode a bomb."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid "Pressing the <guiicon>yellow smiley</guiicon> will start a new game."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"These are the default settings. The mouse buttons can be reprogrammed. For more "
"information, see the section entitled <link linkend=\"prefs\">"
"Game Options</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:120
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>The &kmines; Screen</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:123
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The &kmines; Screen</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:127
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The &kmines; Screen</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kmines; screen consists of:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:134
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A Box showing you the number of mines still left to be marked. Every time you "
"flag a bomb site, this number will decrease by one."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:136
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This box does not determine if you are right or wrong, but only how many mines "
"you need to theoretically mark before you are done with this game."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:139
#, no-c-format
msgid "In this example, there are 40 mines to be marked."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:140
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A Yellow Smiley Face. Clicking this will start a new game. If you lose the "
"game, it will become a frown."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:142
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The box on the right shows how much time this round has taken. The shortest "
"time for each level is listed as the high score."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:145
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The playing area. This will vary in size depending on the difficulty level of "
"the game. In this example, it consists of 256 squares. This is where you play "
"the game."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:155
#, no-c-format
msgid "Game Options"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:156
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The options to &kmines; are set by selecting <menuchoice> <guimenu>"
"Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configure &kmines;</guimenuitem> </menuchoice> "
"from the menubar. This will bring up a dialog box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:161
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>&kmines; Preferences</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:164
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>&kmines; Preferences</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:168
#, no-c-format
msgid "This dialog box is divided into three sections."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:172
#, no-c-format
msgid "Game"
msgstr "Jòc"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:174
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The first option, labeled <guilabel>Enable ? mark</guilabel>"
", determines whether you can mark squares as <quote>questionable</quote>"
". If this option is checked, then right clicking the mouse will first cause a "
"square to be flagged. If you right click again on the same square, the flag "
"will change to a <guiicon>?</guiicon>, to indicate you don't know if there is a "
"bomb there or not. If you click again, the square will change back to blank."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:182
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If there is not a mark in front of this option, the first <mousebutton>"
"right</mousebutton> mouse click will change the square to a red flag. The "
"second will make it blank again, thus skipping the <guiicon>?</guiicon> symbol."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:187
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The next option down, labeled <guilabel>Enable keyboard</guilabel>"
", determines if the keyboard shortcuts will work while playing the game. The "
"default keyboard shortcuts are given in <xref linkend=\"keys\"/>"
", and can be changed by selecting <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu>"
"<guimenuitem>Configure Shortcuts...</guimenuitem></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:193
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The only keyboard shortcuts affected are those responsible for playing the "
"game. Keyboard commands such as <guimenuitem>New Game</guimenuitem> "
"and <guimenuitem>Quit</guimenuitem>, still work, regardless of this option."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:199
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Pause if windows loses focus</guilabel> "
"option will automatically pause the game if the &kmines; window loses focus. "
"When the game is paused, the gameboard disappears, so you cannot use pausing "
"the game as a way to cheat!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:204
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>\"Magic\" reveal</guilabel> option switches on <quote>"
"Magic reveal</quote> mode. In this mode, &kmines; does most of the gameplay for "
"you: If you have uncovered enough squares to be able to tell with certainty "
"that a square contains a mine, &kmines; will automatically mark it as a mine, "
"and perform an autoreveal on squares for which it has marked the correct number "
"of mines. Note that when you have this mode switched on, your scores do not "
"count as highs cores."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:213
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The last section of this tab allows you to change the action of each of the "
"three mouse buttons. Your options are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:218
#, no-c-format
msgid "Reveal"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:219
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will reveal the contents of the square. If there is no bomb, then a number "
"will appear. If there is a bomb under that square, then the bomb will explode, "
"and the game will be over."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:228
#, no-c-format
msgid "Autoreveal"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:229
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Clicking on a square with this button will automatically reveal all neighboring "
"squares that are not marked with red flags. If one of those neighboring squares "
"has a bomb under it, the bomb will explode, and the game will be over."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:236
#, no-c-format
msgid "Toggle Flag"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:237
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Clicking with this button on a square will cycle through blank, red flag, and "
"question mark."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:242
#, no-c-format
msgid "Toggle ? Flag"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:243
#, no-c-format
msgid "Clicking with this button on a square will mark/unmark with a question mark."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:251
#, no-c-format
msgid "Appearance"
msgstr "Aparéncia"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:253
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The top three color buttons determine the <guilabel>Flag Color</guilabel>"
", <guilabel>Explosion Color</guilabel> and <guilabel>Error Color</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:257
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The rest of this page is concerned with mines colors. To adjust, simply click "
"the color button beside each description, and select the new color."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:264
#, no-c-format
msgid "Custom Game"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:266
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Finally, if you are not finding the existing configurations challenging enough, "
"you can set up a custom game here. Use the sliders to change the <guilabel>"
"Width</guilabel>, <guilabel>Height</guilabel>, and the percentage of the board "
"covered with <guilabel>Mines</guilabel>. The default game has 15 percent of the "
"board covered, so there is plenty of room to make the game harder."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:277
#, no-c-format
msgid "Saving your changes"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:278
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once your changes are complete, click <guibutton>OK</guibutton> "
"to make them permanent."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:281
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to abandon your changes, click <guibutton>Cancel</guibutton> "
"to abort the changes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:284
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you click on <guilabel>Defaults</guilabel>, the default settings will be "
"restored. Click <guilabel>OK</guilabel> to make these default changes "
"permanent, or edit the settings some more."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:295
#, no-c-format
msgid "Commands/Keyboard Shortcuts"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:297
#, no-c-format
msgid "The following sections briefly describe each menubar option."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:300
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Game</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:302
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guimenu>Game</guimenu> menu consists of 4 options."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:306
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>N</keycap></keycombo> "
"</shortcut> <guimenu>Game</guimenu> <guimenuitem>New</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:312
#, no-c-format
msgid "Starts a new game."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:316
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycap>P</keycap> </shortcut> <guimenu>Game</guimenu> <guimenuitem>"
"Pause</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:322
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Pauses or resumes the game. This will hide the board (no cheating), and give "
"you a button to press when you want to continue this game."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:328
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>H</keycap></keycombo> "
"</shortcut> <guimenu>Game</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Show Highscores</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:334
#, no-c-format
msgid "This shows you the high score (the shortest time) for each difficulty level."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:339
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>Q</keycap></keycombo> "
"</shortcut> <guimenu>Game</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Quit</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:345
#, no-c-format
msgid "<action>Quits</action> &kmines;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:350
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Move</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:354
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycap>H</keycap> </shortcut> <guimenu>Move</guimenu> <guimenuitem>"
"Hint</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:360
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you use this item, you will get a hint about where you should click next. If "
"you do that your score will not be added to the high-scores."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:366
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Move</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Solve</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:369
#, no-c-format
msgid "This item tries to solve the current game."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:374
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Move</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Solving Rate...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:377
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This item shows a dialog that calculates the solving rate for the current game "
"type."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:382
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Move</guimenu> <guimenuitem>View Log</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:385
#, no-c-format
msgid "This item shows a dialog with the log of the last game."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:390
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Move</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Replay Log</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:393
#, no-c-format
msgid "This item replays the current log."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:398
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Move</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Save Log...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:401
#, no-c-format
msgid "This item shows a dialog to save the current log."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:406
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Move</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Load Log...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:409
#, no-c-format
msgid "This item shows a dialog to load a log."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:416
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:420
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>+</keycap></keycombo> "
"</shortcut> <guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Zoom In</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:426
#, no-c-format
msgid "Increase the size of the gameplay canvas."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:431
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>-</keycap></keycombo> "
"</shortcut> <guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Zoom Out</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:437
#, no-c-format
msgid "Decrease the size of the gameplay canvas."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:444
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:447
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Show Menubar</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:450
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If there is a check in front of this option, then the menubar will be visible. "
"Selecting this option, hides the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:452
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To restore a hidden menubar, click outside the game play area, with the right "
"mouse button. This will bring up a small sub-menu. Simply select <guimenuitem>"
"Show Menubar</guimenuitem> from this sub-menu, and the menubar will be visible "
"again."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:459
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guisubmenu>Choose Game Type</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:464
#, no-c-format
msgid "Lets you set the difficulty level from a sub-menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:465
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are three default levels of difficulty: <guimenuitem>Easy</guimenuitem> "
"(64 squares, 10 mines), <guimenuitem>Normal</guimenuitem> "
"(256 squares, 40 mines), and <guimenuitem>Expert</guimenuitem> "
"(480 squares, 99 mines). There is also a <guimenuitem>Custom...</guimenuitem> "
"level settings."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:470
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you select <guimenuitem>Custom...</guimenuitem>, then the settings you have "
"configured in the <guimenuitem>Configure &kmines;</guimenuitem> "
"dialog will be used."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:476
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure Shortcuts...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:478
#, no-c-format
msgid "This item lets you change the keyboard shortcuts used by &kmines;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:482
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure Notifications...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:484
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This item displays a standard &kde; notifications configuration dialog, where "
"you can change the notifications (sounds, visible messages, &etc;) used by "
"&kmines;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:490
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure Highscores...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:492
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On the <guilabel>Main</guilabel> tab you can change your <guilabel>"
"Nickname</guilabel> and add a cute <guilabel>Comment</guilabel> "
"about yourself, to show in the high score table. You can also activate the "
"<guilabel>World-wide highscores enabled</guilabel> checkbox, and share your "
"skill at &kmines; across the world with an online high score server. If you are "
"connected to the Internet, &kmines; will send your score automatically at the "
"end of the game to the high score web server (kmines.sf.net)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:500
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Advanced</guilabel> tab displays your <guilabel>"
"Registration Data</guilabel> on kmines.sf.net, your <guilabel>"
"Nickname:</guilabel> from the <guilabel>Main</guilabel> tab and the <guilabel>"
"Key:</guilabel>. This key was generated when you registered on kmines.sf.net by "
"selecting <guilabel>World-wide high scores enabled</guilabel> "
"the first time. The registration key is used in conjunction with the nickname "
"to identify uniquely users, but users cannot have the same nickname. Click on "
"the <guibutton>Remove</guibutton> button to delete you from the world high "
"scores list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
